# Sentinel IoT Platform — Mosquitto Per-User Topic ACL
#
# Requires password_file (allow_anonymous false) so that Mosquitto knows
# which username each client has authenticated as.
#
# Mosquitto 2.0: topics not matched by a user's rules are DENIED by default.
#
# To add a real per-device account (replacing the shared sentinel-device role):
#   1. Add `mosquitto_passwd -b /mosquitto/config/passwd sensor-NNN <pass>` in docker-entrypoint.sh
#   2. Add a per-device block below:
#      user sensor-NNN
#      topic write factory/telemetry

# ── Backend service account ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Subscribes to inbound telemetry, publishes rejected messages to DLQ,
# and publishes to the health topic used by the Docker healthcheck.
user sentinel-backend
topic read  factory/telemetry
topic write factory/telemetry/dlq
topic read  factory/telemetry/dlq
topic write sentinel/health

# ── Device / simulator account ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Publish-only to the telemetry topic.
# Cannot subscribe to any topic and cannot touch the DLQ.
user sentinel-device
topic write factory/telemetry
